            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32289",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "html/template: golang: html/template: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) via improper context and brace depth tracking in JS template literals"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Context was not properly tracked across template branches for JS template literals, leading to possibly incorrect escaping of content when branches were used. Additionally template actions within JS template literals did not properly track the brace depth, leading to incorrect escaping being applied. These issues could cause actions within JS template literals to be incorrectly or improperly escaped, leading to XSS vulnerabilities."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32289",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-32289\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.9, 1.26.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-32289](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32289)\nContext was not properly tracked across template branches for JS template literals, leading to possibly incorrect escaping of content when branches were used. Additionally template actions within JS template literals did not properly track the brace depth, leading to incorrect escaping being applied. These issues could cause actions within JS template literals to be incorrectly or improperly escaped, leading to XSS vulnerabilities.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-32289**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|stdlib|1.25.9, 1.26.2|[CVE-2026-32289](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32289)|\n\nContext was not properly tracked across template branches for JS template literals, leading to possibly incorrect escaping of content when branches were used. Additionally template actions within JS template literals did not properly track the brace depth, leading to incorrect escaping being applied. These issues could cause actions within JS template literals to be incorrectly or improperly escaped, leading to XSS vulnerabilities."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39826",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "html/template: golang: html/template: Cross-site scripting due to incorrect script tag escaping"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If a trusted template author were to write a \u003cscript\u003e tag containing an empty 'type' attribute or a 'type' attribute with an ASCII whitespace, the execution of the template would incorrectly escape any data passed into the \u003cscript\u003e block."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39826",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39826\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.10, 1.26.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-39826](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39826)\nIf a trusted template author were to write a \u003cscript\u003e tag containing an empty 'type' attribute or a 'type' attribute with an ASCII whitespace, the execution of the template would incorrectly escape any data passed into the \u003cscript\u003e block.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39826**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|stdlib|1.25.10, 1.26.3|[CVE-2026-39826](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39826)|\n\nIf a trusted template author were to write a \u003cscript\u003e tag containing an empty 'type' attribute or a 'type' attribute with an ASCII whitespace, the execution of the template would incorrectly escape any data passed into the \u003cscript\u003e block."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27139",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "os: FileInfo can escape from a Root in golang os module"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened. The impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27139",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-27139\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.8, 1.26.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-27139](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27139)\nOn Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened. The impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-27139**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|stdlib|1.25.8, 1.26.1|[CVE-2026-27139](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27139)|\n\nOn Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened. The impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39822",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symli ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39822\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.12, 1.26.5, 1.27.0-rc.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-39822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822)\nOn Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39822**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|stdlib|1.25.12, 1.26.5, 1.27.0-rc.2|[CVE-2026-39822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822)|\n\nOn Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
